WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.341
We know that fiber is a main ingredient

2
00:00:04.341 --> 00:00:06.480
for creating a healthy microbiome.

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.105
That's really not up for debate.

4
00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:10.780
(upbeat music)

5
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.593
It's becoming more and more clear as time goes on

6
00:00:13.593 --> 00:00:15.834
that the microbes in our gut

7
00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:20.449
have way more control over our body's biological processes

8
00:00:20.449 --> 00:00:24.300
than we originally thought or might like to believe,

9
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.551
including, as it turns out, immune system functionality,

10
00:00:27.551 --> 00:00:30.930
our resistance to infection and illness.

11
00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.505
If your complimentive gut bacteria are off

12
00:00:33.505 --> 00:00:35.620
and you don't have a healthy microbiome,

13
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.535
your immune system might not trigger

14
00:00:38.535 --> 00:00:42.660
that release of virus slaying capabilities.

15
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.310
To better understand this connection

16
00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.340
between our microbiome and our immune system,

17
00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.949
I sat down with Robynne Chutkan MD.

18
00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.655
Robynne is a board certified gastroenterologist

19
00:00:52.655 --> 00:00:56.690
who serves on the faculty of Georgetown University Hospital.

20
00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:00.195
She is the founder of the Digestive Center for Wellness,

21
00:01:00.195 --> 00:01:02.317
as well as the author of the books,

22
00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:06.810
"Gutbliss: Microbiome Solution," "the Bloat Cure,"

23
00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.720
and her most recent, "the Anti-Viral Gut,"

24
00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.450
which is the central topic of this conversation,

25
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.843
and offers practical advice

26
00:01:13.843 --> 00:01:18.843
for optimizing diet, exercise, sleep, and time outdoors

27
00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:23.700
to boost the body's defenses and our overall health.

28
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:24.810
Most of the immune system

29
00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.330
is physically located in your gut,

30
00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:31.110
about 70% to 80% of it, and there's constant communication,

31
00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.770
so the gut bacteria actually guide that immune response.

32
00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.950
They're constantly sending signals to the immune cells

33
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:38.790
to tell 'em what to do.

34
00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.520
We've talked a lot about the microbiome on this podcast,

35
00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.810
